{"t": 1794107585.2242157, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Fixed the failing `contract-tests` check on this PR.\n\n**Cause:** `payments/fees.py` computed the fee with binary floats (`round(amount * 0.01 * 100, 2)`). The float nearest to `2.675` is actually `2.67499999...`, so `fee(2.675)` rounded down to `2.67` instead of up to `2.68`.\n\n**Change:** the calculation now uses `Decimal` on the exact decimal value and quantizes with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, per the card-network contract in PAY-88 (exact decimal values, half-up to cents):\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\n_CENTS = Decimal(\"0.01\")\n\n\ndef fee(amount: float) -> float:\n    exact = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * Decimal(\"100\")\n    return float(exact.quantize(_CENTS, rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```\n\n**Verification:** `fee(2.675) == 2.68` now holds, and existing behaviour is unchanged (`fee(100.0) == 100.0`). The full local test suite plus the contract assertion pass.\n\nNote: I re-ran the failed job; the check run may need a fresh push/webhook to report the new conclusion.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
